## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design real-time non-rigid 3D reconstruction from monocular input, integrating differentiable rendering and on-device adaptation—critical for AR try-on. It also probes data strategy, evaluation, and edge-latency trade-offs in a commercial retail context.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular non-rigid 3D reconstruction with deformable garments
- Differentiable rendering and photometric consistency
- Temporal fusion for stability
- 5-shot on-device adaptation for unseen fabrics
- Edge latency and data strategy (synthetic+real)

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(frame, params){
  const latent = encoder(frame, params.enc);
  const mesh = deformableMesh(latent, params.shape);
  const render = renderer(mesh, params.tex);
  const loss = photometric(render, frame) + temporal(mesh);
  return {mesh, loss};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle occlusion or loose fabrics?
- How evaluate mesh quality vs. latency?
- How would you construct synthetic data for textiles?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes the ability to design real-time 3D scene understanding from monocular video in crowded environments, focusing on dynamic occupancy rather than static poses. It tests architectural choices, data strategy, and on-device adaptation under latency constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D occupancy mapping in dynamic scenes
- Temporal fusion and uncertainty estimation
- On-device 5-shot adaptation for unseen objects and people
- Privacy-preserving synthetic data pipelines and domain randomization
- Edge GPU optimization and latency budgeting

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: simple occupancy loss combining BCE and temporal consistency
function occupancyLoss(logits, target, mask, prevLogits){
  // logits/target/mask shapes: [B, X, Y, Z]
  const bce = binaryCrossEntropy(logits, target, mask);
  const temporal = meanSquaredError(logits, prevLogits, mask);
  return bce + 0.1 * temporal;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate robustness to occlusions and rapid appearance changes?
- How would you extend to multiple RGB sensors and fuse viewpoints?

